Note: this is a *modified* MIT license — condition (2) is an addition, so this
is not the OSI-approved "MIT License", and tooling that expects verbatim MIT
should treat it as a custom license.

The attribution clause was prompted by issue #1
(https://github.com/Kuberwastaken/cookie/issues/1) — thanks to @ZiClaud for the
nudge to license this properly. That issue proposed AGPL; this takes the
attribution-first path instead: the code stays freely reusable for learning and
awareness, while anyone who actually ships it has to say where it came from.
